## 8. Automated Device Enrollment (ADE) instances and prestages

### ADE instances

- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/v1/device-enrollments`
- **Privilege:** **Read Device Enrollment Program Instances** (https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/get_v1-device-enrollments.md; [PD])
- **Parameters:** `page`, `page-size`, `sort` (default `id:asc`); no filter
- **Fields** (all strings): `id`, `name`, `supervisionIdentityId`, `siteId`, `serverName`, `serverUuid`, `adminId`, `orgName`, `orgEmail`, `orgPhone`, `orgAddress`, `tokenExpirationDate`
- **Sync state:** `/v1/device-enrollments/syncs` and `/v1/device-enrollments/{id}/syncs/latest`, same privilege [PD]

### Computer prestages

- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/v3/computer-prestages`
- **Privilege:** **Read Computer PreStage Enrollments** (https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/get_v3-computer-prestages.md; [PD])
- **Parameters:** `page`, `page-size`, `sort` (default `id:desc`); no filter
- **Fields:**
  - booleans: `mandatory`, `mdmRemovable`, `requireAuthentication`, `preventActivationLock`, `enableDeviceBasedActivationLock`, `autoAdvanceSetup`, `defaultPrestage`, `keepExistingSiteMembership`, `keepExistingLocationInformation`, `installProfilesDuringSetup`, `enableRecoveryLock`, `rotateRecoveryLockPassword`, `pssoEnabled`
  - strings: `displayName`, `authenticationPrompt`, `deviceEnrollmentProgramInstanceId`, `enrollmentSiteId`, `siteId`, `profileUuid`
  - `skipSetupItems`: object
  - `recoveryLockPasswordType`: enum `MANUAL`, `RANDOM`
  - `prestageMinimumOsTargetVersionType`: enum `NO_ENFORCEMENT`, `MINIMUM_OS_LATEST_VERSION`, `MINIMUM_OS_LATEST_MAJOR_VERSION`, `MINIMUM_OS_LATEST_MINOR_VERSION`, `MINIMUM_OS_SPECIFIC_VERSION`, plus `minimumOsSpecificVersion`
  - `accountSettings{payloadConfigured, localAdminAccountEnabled, adminUsername, hiddenAdminAccount, localUserManaged, userAccountType (ADMINISTRATOR/STANDARD/SKIP, default STANDARD), preventPrefillInfoFromModification, prefill…}`
- **No `enabled` field.** Scope is at `/api/v2/computer-prestages/scope` (same privilege [PD]).
- **Sample (illustrative):** `{"totalCount":1,"results":[{"id":"1","displayName":"Corp Macs","mandatory":true,"mdmRemovable":false,"requireAuthentication":true,"deviceEnrollmentProgramInstanceId":"5","enableRecoveryLock":true,"recoveryLockPasswordType":"RANDOM","accountSettings":{"userAccountType":"STANDARD"}}]}`

### Mobile prestages

- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/v3/mobile-device-prestages`
- **Privilege:** **Read Mobile Device PreStage Enrollments**. `/v2/mobile-device-prestages` was deprecated on 2025-06-30 [PD]. Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/get_v3-mobile-device-prestages.md
- **Parameters:** sort default `id:desc`
- **Fields:**
  - shared with computer prestages: `mandatory`, `mdmRemovable`, `requireAuthentication`, `preventActivationLock`, `enableDeviceBasedActivationLock`, `autoAdvanceSetup`, `defaultPrestage`
  - booleans: `supervised`, `allowPairing`, `multiUser`, `configureDeviceBeforeSetupAssistant`, `temporarySessionOnly`, `enforceTemporarySessionTimeout`, `enforceUserSessionTimeout`, `rtsEnabled`
  - integer: `maximumSharedAccounts`
  - minimum OS: `prestageMinimumOsTargetVersionTypeIos` and `prestageMinimumOsTargetVersionTypeIpad`

## 9. Computer configuration profiles

- **Classic only.** The JPAPI index has no macOS configuration-profile list or read endpoint (https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/jamf-pro-api/llms.txt).
- **List:** `GET /JSSResource/osxconfigurationprofiles` returns `{id, name}` entries. Send `Accept: application/json` for JSON. Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/findosxconfigurationprofiles.md
- **Detail:** `GET /JSSResource/osxconfigurationprofiles/id/{id}` returns `os_x_configuration_profile` with:
  - `general{id, name, description, site, category, distribution_method ("Install Automatically"|"Make Available in Self Service"), user_removable (bool), level ("computer"|"user"), uuid, redeploy_on_update (string, e.g. "Newly Assigned"), payloads (string)}`
  - `scope{all_computers, all_jss_users, computers, buildings, departments, computer_groups, jss_users, jss_user_groups, limitations, exclusions}`
  - `self_service{...}`
  - Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/findosxconfigurationprofilesbyid.md (Classic spec 11.32.0)
- **Subset reads:** the index also lists `findosxconfigurationprofilesbyidsubset` ("Finds a subset of data"). Requesting only the General and Scope subsets may make each call smaller. The exact subset syntax is UNVERIFIED.
- **Privilege:** "Read - macOS Configuration Profiles" [CP]. The API role string "Read macOS Configuration Profiles" appears in third-party guides (see Conventions) but is UNVERIFIED in Jamf's own documentation.
- **Paging:** none. The pack needs one call per profile (N+1 calls).
- **Payloads:** `payloads` is a string. That it holds an XML plist is UNVERIFIED in the spec but is standard. Parse it and match `PayloadType`:
  - FileVault: `com.apple.MCX.FileVault2`; escrow: `com.apple.security.FDERecoveryKeyEscrow`
  - Firewall: `com.apple.security.firewall`
- **Change Management:** no API was found for its settings or logs in the JPAPI or Classic index.
  - "The option to log changes to a log file or a syslog server is only available for on-premise environments." The file is `JAMFChangeManagement.log`. On Jamf Cloud, changes "are automatically displayed in the Change Management settings and cannot be exported". Source: https://learn.jamf.com/r/en-US/jamf-pro-documentation-current/Change_Management
  - Jamf Log Stream is "available only to customers of the Jamf Cloud Premium offering". It sends Change Management and Access logs to Splunk, Amazon S3, Datadog or an HTTPS endpoint. Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/docs/jamf-log-stream.md
  - An API to check whether Log Stream is configured is UNVERIFIED and none was found.
  - STIG V-241793 (medium) requires logs to be transferred to another server.
- **Log flushing (retention):** `GET /api/v1/log-flushing` returns `{retentionPolicies: [{displayName, qualifier, retentionPeriod: integer, retentionPeriodUnit: string}], hourOfDay: integer}`.
  - `retentionPeriodUnit` is a plain string described as "eg: DAY, WEEK, MONTH, YEAR", not a declared enum.
  - Privilege: **Read Retention Policy**. Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/get_v1-log-flushing.md
- **Webhooks (Classic only):**
  - `GET /JSSResource/webhooks` and `/webhooks/id/{id}` return:
    - `id`, `name`, `enabled`, `url`
    - `content_type` (`text/xml`|`application/json`)
    - `event` (enum, 18 values including `RestAPIOperation`, `ComputerAdded`, `SCEPChallenge`)
    - `connection_timeout`, `read_timeout`
    - `authentication_type` (`NONE`|`BASIC`)
    - `username`, `password`, `enable_display_fields_for_group_object`, `display_fields`
  - Privilege: "Read - Webhooks" [CP]
  - Sources: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/findwebhooks.md and https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/findwebhooksbyid.md
  - The schema includes `password`. Whether a GET returns it in clear text is UNVERIFIED. The pack should drop the field.
  - Checks this enables: webhook URLs that are not HTTPS, and `authentication_type == NONE`.
- **Object history:** per-object history exists, for example `/v1/device-enrollments/{id}/history` and `/v1/jamf-pro-server-url/history`, each needing its object's Read privilege [PD].
- **Login banner (STIG V-241794, low):** `GET /api/v1/login-customization` needs authentication but no privilege [PD].
  - It returns `LoginContent{includeCustomDisclaimer, disclaimerHeading, disclaimerMainText, actionText, rampInstance, fedRampInstance, highComplianceInstance}`.
  - Source: https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/reference/get_v1-login-customization.md
- **Health notifications:** `GET /api/v1/notifications` needs authentication but no privilege [PD]. It returns `[{type, id, params}]`.
  - The `type` enum includes `INSECURE_LDAP`, `PUSH_CERT_WILL_EXPIRE`, `PUSH_CERT_EXPIRED`, `APNS_CERT_REVOKED`, `DEP_INSTANCE_WILL_EXPIRE`, `DEP_INSTANCE_EXPIRED`, `SSO_CERT_WILL_EXPIRE`, `SSO_CERT_EXPIRED`, `SSO_IDP_CERT_WILL_EXPIRE`, `SSO_IDP_CERT_EXPIRED`, `TOMCAT_SSL_CERT_WILL_EXPIRE`, `TOMCAT_SSL_CERT_EXPIRED`, `BUILT_IN_CA_EXPIRING`, `BUILT_IN_CA_EXPIRED`, `VPP_TOKEN_REVOKED`, `USER_INITIATED_ENROLLMENT_MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_SECURITY_ISSUE`, `POLICY_MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_PAYLOAD_SECURITY_SINGLE`, `POLICY_MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_PAYLOAD_SECURITY_MULTIPLE` and `SAML_RESPONSE_ASSERTION_SIGNING_REQUIRED`.
